diff --git a/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md b/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md
index a31946d95..0877d3b03 100644
--- a/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md
+++ b/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md
@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@
 - `new AISessionsPage({ meta, classic: true })` draws the old all-controls-in-rows layout (`sessions/v/classic/`); its `data_url` getter strips a trailing `v/classic/` so every data file and row link still points at the real list.
 - A rail card (`AISessionView` with `card: true`) shows four things: title, the one cost line, "N child sessions · M in all" and state. The rail lists root sessions only: `AISessionsPage.roots_for_cards` hides a row whose parent is in the list, and switching Table/Rail re-applies the grid.
 - `AISessionDetail.js` · `AISessionConversation.js` · `AISessionCoverage.js` · `AISessionTrace.js` — a session's own page and its tabs. A clicked row opens that session's full page in place of the list (previews plus full detail views: [design/navigation](/framework/design/navigation/readme.md)); the sessions page no longer calls `columns()`. A named agent's url (`/framework/ai/sessions/<name>/`, a `reviewer-*` or `minion-*` row) resolves the name to its session through Servex's live agent list (`AISessionDetail.agent_row`), and every load asks the folder listing first, so the page never asks for a file that is not there.
-- The session page's tabs are **Overview · Board · Tasks · Chat**, then Coverage, Cost, Models and tokens, Related. `?tab=work` opens Tasks and `?tab=conversation` opens Chat. Above the tabs sits the sticky stats bar (`SessionStats.js`: cost, model, running for, done X of Y, the one segmented bar); it reads the tree `SessionWork` loads, so one load serves the bar, the Overview and the Tasks tab. **A session's cost is one line from one function, `AICost.cost_line`: "$282 this tab · $1035 with children"** ("this session" when it is not a VS Code tab). The Cost tile, the Sessions list's Cost cell and its rail card all draw it. The own figure is the summary's `cost.own.usd` (before it arrives, the day snapshot's `usd`); "with children" is `summary.cost.total`, which the item tool computes (`AICost.summary(AICost.session_url(id))`, one cached answer per session for every surface), never `SessionWork`'s own sum. The list never asks for every row: it shows an answer already here, else a small "with children …" button that asks for that one row. Clicking the Cost tile opens the Cost tab, whose first block lists every child session behind the total (`AICost.draw_session`). **The Overview tab is `SessionOutlineView.js` (+ `SessionOutline.css`, prefix `soutline-`), drawn from `SessionOutline.js`, which has no DOM and is tested by `node SessionOutline.test.mjs`.** It groups the session's work by child session: one box per child (name linking to that child's own page, state, model, an `AICost` cost line, "N of M done") holding the tasks whose folder is the child's or below it, then "This session's own work", sub-grouped by the prompt that asked for it (`SessionOutline.source(session)` is the one place that join lives) with "Other work" for the rest. The children are the union, de-duplicated by session id, of the `sessions` lines of `session.jsonl`, the tree nodes that carry `session`, the day snapshot's `links.children`, and the snapshots whose `parent` is this session's agent; groups are ranked by cost × 0.5^(age days ÷ 2) plus recency, with a "newest first" toggle. A task is one full-width row (open, running, done and dropped icons; the child session's model, cost and state; subtasks folded in), and a done task opens its proof in place. The rows are the Overview's own markup (`SessionOutlineView.item`), not `TaskView`: they carry no start/pause/stop buttons (those live on `TaskView` rows in the Tasks tab), and a folder-only task has no `Task` object for `TaskView` to draw. `SessionTasks` hands it each replay through `on_session`, and the view redraws live. `SessionFeed.js` (+ `SessionFeed.css`, prefix `sfeed-`) is the older flat list and is no longer wired in. `SessionOverview.js` draws the Board tab's four cards side by side (Open, Project, Done, Dropped), with the phone's classes (`MobileRow`, `MobileTaskRow`, `mob-` CSS); `SessionTaskRow.js` is the phone's task row that opens the task's full page and shows its cost. Their styles, and the full-screen mode with two floating buttons (`AISessionDetail.full_screen`, `?full`), are `SessionOverview.css` (prefix `sov-`).
