+- **The Timeline tab** (`?tab=timeline`) is `SessionTimeline.js` (+ `SessionTimeline.css`, prefix `stl-`): everything the session recorded in time order, newest at the bottom, the list opening scrolled to the bottom. One compact row per event (time, icon, one or two lines): each line of `session.jsonl` is one row (task added and done, child session started, note, decision, review, commit, session start and stop, log and tag lines), each prompt of `prompts.jsonl` is one row (its subject, the raw words one click down), and each child session that has landed adds one (name linked with `AICost.session_url`, its state, model and `AICost.cost_line`, never summed here). The rows are built with no DOM by `SessionTimelineRows.js`, tested by `node SessionTimeline.test.mjs` (rows drawn = record lines + distinct prompts + landed children, counted by hand on a fixture; the page shows the same number as `data-total`). It fetches nothing of its own for the record: `AISessionDetail` feeds it `SessionTasks`' replay (`on_session(session, lines)`), the Overview's child list (`SessionOutlineView`'s `on_draw`) and its own prompt tail (`SessionTimeline.Tail`, a `JSONL` that follows `prompts.jsonl`), so new lines appear without a reload. **Filters ▾** is a checkbox per kind in the same popover the Sessions list header uses (`SessionPopover.open(anchor, content, cls)`, which wraps `ux/Popover` and the `sessions-pop` skin); log and tag lines are off until ticked. With no record the tab shows the prompts alone, or one plain sentence.
